# Cloudflare Pages redirect map — DTLM Architect
#
# Brief §9.2: "Build a redirect map from old URLs to new... Losing project and
# press URLs means losing accumulated search ranking."
#
# STATUS: mostly empty, and that is currently correct.
#
# The client decided on 14 Aug 2026 to PRESERVE the existing WordPress URL
# structure rather than move to the /projects/ paths proposed in brief §4:
#
#     /works/                    stays /works/
#     /portfolio/[slug]/         stays /portfolio/[slug]/
#     /project-type/[typology]/  stays /project-type/[typology]/
#     /team/                     stays /team/
#
# Because those URLs do not change, they need no redirects. That decision was
# taken partly to remove the risk created by an incomplete URL inventory — the
# Phase 0 crawl could not enumerate 30 of the 34 project slugs, because the
# existing site's robots.txt was returning HTTP 508.
#
# WHAT STILL NEEDS DOING BEFORE LAUNCH
#
# 1. The WordPress news archive at /category/updates/ (and its paginated pages)
#    has no equivalent, because §5 Option 2 replaces the post archive with a
#    single curated page. Every individual post URL under it needs a redirect.
#    Those URLs are NOT yet known — see the Phase 0 audit.
#
# 2. Confirm every /portfolio/ slug in src/content/projects/*.md matches the
#    live site exactly. A mismatched slug silently breaks an indexed URL.
#
# 3. Run a crawl of the live site immediately before cutover and diff it
#    against the built site's sitemap. Anything in the first list and not the
#    second needs a line here.

# --- News archive -----------------------------------------------------------
# The archive index and its pagination collapse onto the curated press page.
/category/updates/            /news/   301
/category/updates/page/*      /news/   301

